# Round files that predate the one-file-per-round convention
#
# The convention (scripts/lib/consultation-rounds.sh) is: a consultation that
# goes more than one round is stored as `<pr>.md` carrying the latest round,
# linking every earlier round as `<pr>-round<N>.md`. It was adopted on
# 2026-08-02, after PR #150 was reviewed twice in one file and the consultation
# gate correctly read the first verdict it found.
#
# The rounds below were filed before that. They are whole and unedited; what
# they lack is a `<pr>.md` primary tying them together, because at the time the
# last round WAS the primary and there was nothing to tie.
#
# Entries are matched literally, one filename per line. This register is for
# files that already exist — it is not a way to file a new round without a
# primary, and a round created after 2026-08-02 that lands here should be
# refused in review rather than registered.
#
# Nothing here may be deleted or shortened. That is checked separately and
# against git history, not against this list.

